  note = {Opened: author preprint submitted 15 June 2000, complete Theorem 2.1 and its written proof on pp. 11--12, the preceding residue-complex discussion on pp. 10--11, and complete Theorem 1.3 and Corollary 1.9 written proofs on pp. 3 and 7, read 20 November 2026. The assertion used is cyclicity and index equal to period for prime-to-residue-characteristic Brauer classes over the fraction field of an excellent henselian two-dimensional local domain with separably closed residue field. The local symbol argument and every codimension-one/two case in the written proof were read. Resolution, purity, the residue complex and the cited background theorems remain Known inputs; no fresh recursive proof audit is claimed. The later publication is in Algebra, Arithmetic and Geometry (Mumbai, 2000), Tata Institute of Fundamental Research Studies in Mathematics 16 (2002), pp. 185--217. The locators in the present proof refer explicitly to the opened 20-page preprint, not to an uninspected numbering in that publication. The cyclic splitting field in the proof may ramify along its auxiliary divisor; no etale-splitter or quantitative degree assertion is attributed to the source.}
